--  The contracts that the library checks at run time (amv.gpr and the C
--  projects, which compile the library's sources themselves): the
--  preconditions of the kernels, which reject what a caller must not
--  pass. Everything else (postconditions, ghost code, loop invariants,
--  assertions, predicates) is proved by gnatprove (docs/PROOF.md) and
--  ignored here. The tests (amv_tests.gpr, -gnata, tests/contracts.adc)
--  check every contract but the steps of the proofs, so that each test
--  also compares the code with its contracts (docs/DESIGN.md 9.2).
--
--  The assertion level Tested marks the part of a postcondition that the
--  tests check where another part, at the level Static, is proved only:
--  Post => (Tested => ..., Static => ...). A postcondition cannot mix a
--  level with a plain expression. Both files declare it, and so does
--  every unit that uses it, so that a program that withs the unit reads
--  it with any configuration.

pragma Assertion_Level (Tested);

pragma Assertion_Policy
  (Pre => Check, Post => Ignore, Ghost => Ignore,
   Loop_Invariant => Ignore, Loop_Variant => Ignore, Assert => Ignore,
   Assert_And_Cut => Ignore, Contract_Cases => Ignore,
   Subprogram_Variant => Ignore, Dynamic_Predicate => Ignore,
   Type_Invariant => Ignore, Default_Initial_Condition => Ignore,
   Tested => Ignore);
